WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.300
A map of colours.

2
00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:03.504
A colour wheel is a map of colours.

3
00:00:03.664 --> 00:00:06.682
Red, yellow and blue, the primaries, sit apart.

4
00:00:06.842 --> 00:00:10.372
The colours they make sit between them: orange, green and purple.

5
00:00:11.072 --> 00:00:12.047
Opposites.

6
00:00:12.207 --> 00:00:19.359
Colours straight across from each other are called complementary colours: red and green, blue and orange, yellow and purple.

7
00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:22.212
Side by side, they make each other look brighter.

8
00:00:22.912 --> 00:00:23.980
Mixing opposites.

9
00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:27.763
Mix two colours that sit side by side and you get a bright colour.

10
00:00:27.923 --> 00:00:32.102
Mix two opposites and they cancel each other out, into a dull brown.

11
00:00:32.262 --> 00:00:35.652
Artists use a little of the opposite to calm a colour down.

12
00:00:36.352 --> 00:00:37.560
Choose a scheme.

13
00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:40.692
A colour scheme is the set of colours a picture uses.

14
00:00:40.852 --> 00:00:41.966
Warm for heat.

15
00:00:42.126 --> 00:00:43.287
Cool for calm.

16
00:00:43.447 --> 00:00:45.073
Complementary to stand out.

17
00:00:45.233 --> 00:00:49.645
If a picture is not working, try changing the scheme before you change anything else.
